{{also|Appendix:Variations of "leg"}}
==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|leg}}, {{m|enm|legge}}, from {{der|en|non|leggr|t=leg, calf, bone of the arm or leg, hollow tube, stalk}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*lagjaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*lagwijaz|t=leg, thigh}} (see it for more).

Cognate with {{cog|sco|leg||leg}}, {{cog|is|leggur||leg, limb}}, {{cog|nb|legg||leg}}, {{cog|nn|legg||leg}}, {{cog|sv|lägg||leg, shank, shaft}}, {{cog|da|læg||leg}}, {{cog|lng|lagi||thigh, shank, leg}}, {{cog|la|lacertus||limb, arm}}, {{cog|fa|لنگ|tr=leng}}. Upon borrowing, mostly displaced the native [[Old English]] term {{m|ang|sċanca}} ([[Modern English]] ''[[shank]]'').

