====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[limb]] or [[appendage]] that an animal uses for support or locomotion on land.
#: {{ux|en|Insects have six '''legs'''.}}
# In humans, the lower limb extending from the [[groin]] to the [[ankle]].
#: {{ux|en|Dan won't be able to come to the party, since he broke his '''leg''' last week and is now on crutches.}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The portion of the lower limb of a human that extends from the [[knee]] to the [[ankle]].
# A part of [[garment]], such as a pair of [[trousers]]/[[pants]], that covers a leg.
#: {{ux|en|The left '''leg''' of these jeans has a tear.}}
# A [[rod]][[-like]] [[protrusion]] from an [[inanimate]] object, such as a piece of [[furniture]], supporting it from [[underneath]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''legs''' of a chair or table}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} Something that [[support]]s.
#: {{ux|en|This observation is an important '''leg''' of my argument.}}
# A [[stage]] of a [[journey]], [[race]] etc.
#: {{ux|en|After six days, we're finally in the last '''leg''' of our cross-country trip.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[distance]] that a [[sailing vessel]] does without changing the sails from one side to the other.
# {{lb|en|nautical}} One side of a multiple-sided (often [[triangular]]) [[course]] in a sailing race.
# {{lb|en|sports}} A single [[game]] or [[match]] played in a [[tournament]] or other sporting contest.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=November 11, 2011|author=Rory Houston| title=Estonia 0-4 Republic of Ireland| work=RTE Sport| url=http://www.rte.ie/sport/soccer/2011/1111/estonia_ireland_report.html|
passage=A stunning performance from the Republic of Ireland all but sealed progress to Euro 2012 as they crushed nine-man Estonia 4-0 in the first '''leg''' of the qualifying play-off tie in A Le Coq Arena in Tallinn.}}
# {{lb|en|geometry}} One of the two sides of a [[right triangle]] that is not the [[hypotenuse]].
# {{lb|en|geometry}} One of the two equal sides of an [[isosceles triangle]].
# {{lb|en|geometry}} One of the branches of a [[hyperbola]] or other [[curve]] which [[extend]] outward [[indefinitely]].
# {{lb|en|usually|in plural}} The [[ability]] of something to persist or [[succeed]] over a long period of time.
#: {{ux|en|This proposal has no '''legs'''. Almost everyone opposes it.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2020/feb/02/one-is-a-great-guy-the-other-good-in-bed-who-do-i-choose-mariella-frostrup|title=One is a great guy; the other is good in bed. So who do I choose?|date=2020-02-02|work=The Guardian|passage=I’m trying to go with my head and focus on the first guy, because this could be a relationship with '''legs'''.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|slang|archaic}} A [[disreputable]] [[sporting]] character; a [[blackleg]].
# An extension of a [[steam]] [[boiler]] downward, in the form of a narrow space between vertical plates, sometimes nearly surrounding the furnace and ash pit, and serving to support the boiler; called also [[water leg]].
# In a [[grain elevator]], the case containing the lower part of the belt which carries the buckets.
# {{lb|en|cricket|attributive}} {{n-g|Denotes the [[half]] of the [[field]] on the same side as the [[batsman]]'s [[leg]]s; the [[left]] side for a [[right-handed]] batsman.}}
#: {{syn|en|on}}; {{ant|en|off}}
#: {{ux|en|Ponsonby-Smythe hit a thumping drive through the '''leg''' fielders.}}
# {{lb|en|telephony}} A [[branch]] or [[lateral]] [[circuit]] connecting an [[instrument]] with the main line.
# {{lb|en|electrical}} A branch circuit; one [[phase]] of a [[polyphase]] system.
# {{lb|en|finance}} An underlying [[instrument]] of a [[derivative]]s strategy.
# {{lb|en|US|slang|military}} An army soldier assigned to a paratrooper unit who has not yet been qualified as a paratrooper.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2019|author=Elliot Murphy|title=A Vietnam Story|page=94
|passage=Which was lower than whale shit in the eyes of any paratrooper; it would have been a disgrace to be a '''leg'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} A gesture of [[submission]]; a [[bow]] or [[curtsey]]. Chiefly in phrase {{m|en|make a leg}}.
#* {{RQ:Richardson Clarissa|letter=74|text=Hickman came in, making his '''legs''', and stroking his cravat and ruffles.}}
# {{lb|en|journalism}} A [[column]], as a unit of length of text as laid out.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=Homer L. Hall; Megan Fromm; Aaron Manfull|title=Student Journalism & Media Literacy|page=266
|passage=A '''leg''' is one column of a story. It has two '''legs''' if it is set in two columns and three '''legs''' if it is set in three columns. Avoid '''legs''' longer than 10 inches and shorter than 1 inch.}}
# {{syn of|en|leg up||forming a step for a person's feet with one's hands}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1902|journal=The Idler: An Illustrated Monthly Magazine|volume=21|page=737
|passage=The street was deserted. We acted quickly. Josiah gave me a '''leg'''. I threw my jacket over the broken glass {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|gambling}} An individual [[bet#Noun|bet]] in a [[parlay#Noun|parlay]] {{gl|a series of bets where the stake and winnings are cumulatively carried forward}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Swain Scheps|title=Sports Betting For Dummies|location=Hoboken, N.J.|publisher=w:John Wiley & Sons, Inc.|year=2020|page=265|pageurl=https://books.google.ca/books?id=cFnsDwAAQBAJ&pg=PA265|isbn=978-1-119-74862-5|passage=If one '''leg''' from your 2-way parlay pushes and the other wins, your parlay bet wins and is paid off as if it's a straight bet (paying -110 or whatever the odds were).}}

